<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Because ordinarily you would expect it to be familiar to chemists (and everyone else).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<blockquote>
<p>'HK-Class environmental conversion scenario' comes out of the blue, in the last sentence, with no development. ???</p>
</blockquote>
<p>They gave it to mouse, then discovered the mouse was made of it. Then to a second mouse and discovered that mouse would die without it. Therefore they think that if introduced to the environment it would convert everything.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>And why is it corrosive then?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's corrosive because it is a polar solvent and will form free protons or free hydroxyl ions when in solution with nearly any solute it can dissolve.</p>

